# The same walk from power-on as sync_title, with a different pair of
# characters. sync_title is Pikachu vs Peach and every fix measured against it
# risks being a fix for Pikachu vs Peach: a bone table, a hurtbox count, an
# article, a special move. This case exists so that a change that helps one
# lineup and breaks another is visible as a failure rather than as nothing.
#
#   tools/pc_lockstep.py sync_pair2 --cpu 9,9 --frames 3000 --headless
#
# The character-select route is generated by tools/pc_route.py from the game's
# own icon table and cursor integrator, not authored by hand, so any pair can
# be swapped in by regenerating these lines.
description: Samus vs Donkey Kong from the title screen, in step every frame
rendezvous: 24
route_zero: 187
port_input_lag: 3
scene_skew: 4
ignore: seed
ref_input: 236:+START
ref_input: 240:-START
ref_input: 400:+START
ref_input: 404:-START
ref_input: 760:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 768:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 820:+A
ref_input: 824:-A
ref_input: 950:+A
ref_input: 954:-A
ref_input: 1000:P2:+A
ref_input: 1004:P2:-A
ref_input: 1060:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1096:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1106:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1136:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1146:+A
ref_input: 1150:-A
ref_input: 1206:P2:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1235:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1245:P2:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1281:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
